---
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { SITE } from "@niki/theme/site";
---

<PageHeader
  eyebrow="About"
  title="A pipeline you can verify."
  description="Niki is an open-source project built around one idea: AI-generated code should arrive as evidence — a branch you can review, tests that ran, and a trail of what every agent decided."
  canonicalPath="/about"
/>

<section class="nk-section nk-container">
  <div class="nk-about-grid">
    <div class="nk-about-copy">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Niki is the open-source multi-agent coding pipeline: describe a task, and four independent
        agents — Planner, Coder, Tester, Reviewer — plan, code, test and review it inside hermetic
        sandboxes. What comes back is a verified git branch with the entire decision trail.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's written in Rust as a single binary, licensed Apache-2.0, and built for solo developers
        and small teams who want to delegate multi-file tasks and review a polished result — instead
        of steering an assistant through every edit.
      </p>
      <p>
        The project holds itself to a simple bar: every public claim is reproducible from the
        repository. When reality and copy drift, copy loses.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="nk-about-facts">
      <h3 class="nk-mono">facts</h3>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>What</dt>
          <dd>Multi-agent coding pipeline (CLI + TUI)</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Written in</dt>
          <dd>Rust, edition 2024</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>License</dt>
          <dd>Apache-2.0</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Current release</dt>
          <dd>v{SITE.release.version} ({SITE.release.date})</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Sandbox</dt>
          <dd>Podman / Docker / git-worktree</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Providers</dt>
          <dd>12, BYOK</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Telemetry</dt>
          <dd>None</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="nk-section nk-container" aria-labelledby="name-heading">
  <div class="nk-about-note">
    <h2 id="name-heading">The name</h2>
    <p>
      NIKI carries personal meaning to its founder. It's short, it types fast, and it doesn't
      pretend to be an acronym.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .nk-about-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--nk-space-5);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .nk-about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--nk-space-6);
    }
  }

  .nk-about-copy h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--nk-space-2);
  }

  .nk-about-copy p + p {
    margin-top: var(--nk-space-2);
  }

  .nk-about-copy p {
    color: var(--nk-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .nk-about-facts {
    border: 1px solid var(--nk-surface-border);
    border-radius: var(--nk-radius-card);
    background: var(--nk-bg-1);
    padding: var(--nk-space-3);
    align-self: start;
  }

  .nk-about-facts h3 {
    color: var(--nk-mint);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: var(--nk-space-2);
  }

  .nk-about-facts dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .nk-about-facts dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .nk-about-facts dt {
    color: var(--nk-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--nk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    padding-top: 2px;
  }

  .nk-about-facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--nk-text-secondary);
  }

  .nk-about-note {
    max-width: 560px;
  }

  .nk-about-note h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--nk-space-2);
  }

  .nk-about-note p {
    color: var(--nk-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
